{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne","id":1542047,"title":"[Curseborne] What do you DO in Curseborne?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-13T07:50:33-07:00","id":1542047,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Curseborne] What do you DO in Curseborne?","content":"What do characters actually *do* in Curseborne? Here's some examples to help you along.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-what-do-characters-do/\" target=\"_blank\">https://theonyxpath.com/curseborne-w...characters-do/</a></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T22:40:01-07:00","id":1542097,"title":"","content":"( I will short <b>Curseborne</b> to <b>CB</b> from now on, to not write all the time full gameline name. )<br /> <br /> <b>It was exactly (!!!) the question</b> that was lingering on my mind from first Ashcan of <b>Curseborne</b>. Compared to <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> - what <b>CB </b>is 'direct competitor' - <b>CB</b> do not have clearly defined <i><b>'gameplay loop'</b></i>. ( Or at least I did not seen it in media and press releases to this day ) You know, every <b>CofD</b> game is about SOMETHING you do - <b>VtR</b> is about drinking blood and politics, <b>WtF </b>is about hunting and pack looking over interactions of Flesh &amp; Spirit in territory, <b>MtAw </b>is about uncovering Mysteries. However <b>Curseborne</b> do not seem to have to highly detailed 'gameplay loop'.<br /> <br /> <i>Which is kinda problem</i>, as GM when I sit to prepare chronicle, I start with <b>trying to make main plot idea ABOUT 'gameplay loop'</b>. For example, when I create <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> 2E chronicle, I know I want The Hunt to be main plot line, as literal game is based on it. When I prepare <b>Promethean the Created</b> game, I know it will be about creating Philosophical Stone and 'growing up' of character. I REALLY hope this blog post and final <b>CB</b> corebook will address this 'what is main gameplay loop of gameline' problem.<br /> <br /> More on idea of <b>Gamplay Loops</b> - <a href=\"https://www.makeuseof.com/gameplay-loop-gaming/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.makeuseof.com/gameplay-loop-gaming/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-14-2024, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T10:25:37-07:00","id":1542119,"title":"","content":"It's about shit blowing in your face because you're cursed, so bad things will always happen to you, of all people, because of course.<br /> <br /> To be honest I like it. It's simple, yet versatile and effective.<br /> <br /> But I should note, this game has a greater expectation as it seems that your character is invested in having a somewhat normal life. The Accursed are, at the end of the day, less a monster society apart from everyday life, and more people that just have this additional layer to them.<br /> <br /> Which again, is something I'm liking, a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T16:06:43-07:00","id":1542141,"title":"","content":"So from blog posts I got strong <i><b>'Greater Family</b></i>' vibe of <b>Curseborne</b>. Very similar to <b>Beast the Primordial </b>society in that regards. Chosen family of beings not quite clicking with rest of the world. 'Family Buisness' like they would say Winchesters in <b>Supernatural</b>. 'Family dramas' sound as another big plot legs of <b>CB</b>. Modern media like <b>'House of Ushers'</b> 2023, but also <b>'Dark Shadows' </b>2012<b>.</b> Or even (darker) latino telenovelas ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-25-2024, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T18:05:19-07:00","id":1542151,"title":"","content":"If I may suggest. Instead of comparing Curseborne to the different CoD games, think about it as a different game, with different intentions and different style.<br /> Curseborne is about cursed people that found help/support/sense of belonging in a group of other cursed people. They are not monsters, they are not mythological beings or people from folklore, they are weird in unique ways.<br /> Each family has different things going on, and most of the members of those families are immortals (so they are doing that for a while now), so you may play many different games in the same setting, and with the same group, as they have different tones and objectives related to their families. The elders have all the time in the world, and are ok to let you alone for a while doing your stuff (or even convincing you to do their stuff as if it was your stuff).<br /> Family dramas is one option, getting away from your family looking for yourself is also an option, as is turning the group into your real family instead of the ones that share your curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T01:37:52-07:00","id":1542164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1542151#post1542151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family dramas is one option, getting away from your family looking for yourself is also an option, as is turning the group into your real family instead of the ones that share your curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that are 'family dramas' in my life book \ud83d\ude09 But it's nitpicking really. We have some picture of gameline plots, finally. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> Second 'plot leg' of <b>CB</b> are mysteries, weird places and horror - investigating urban myths and ghost stories. Finding 'what's out there...' - and if it's dangerous, to Accuresed or mortals.<br /> <br /> Both leads to...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1542151#post1542151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may suggest. Instead of comparing Curseborne to the different CoD games, think about it as a different game, with different intentions and different style.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will see, as it really sounds as <b>CB</b> is <b>Beast the Primoridal</b>-ish setting, without it's problematic parts. \ud83d\ude0e And I really mean it's in good way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - interactions between 'monster families', helping your 'cousins', solving weird mysteries about enigmatic places. It all wasin<b> BtP</b>. <b>BtP</b> also had Astral journeys and predation on mortals - <b>CB</b> is free on that, and it can only help gameline. It's less cluttered ( at least in main idea ) and free on problematic themes. ( However, I will miss a bit an Astral equivalent, as it was such good story fodder. ) At least we have much open ended and varied Limilanilties in CB. It will be interesting to look into. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1542151#post1542151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curseborne is about cursed people that found help/support/sense of belonging in a group of other cursed people. They are not monsters, they are not mythological beings or people from folklore, they are weird in unique ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<i>Not from mythology or folklore' </i>- ( Points to <b>Hungry </b>and <b>Primals</b> Families we know about in silence. )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1542151#post1542151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most of the members of those families are immortals (so they are doing that for a while now),</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed info on immortality of Family memebers - Where it was pointed? Would gladly read on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2024, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T14:21:55-07:00","id":1542270,"title":"","content":"The point is that they don\u2019t see themselves as the denizens of Scion do. They are cursed, and that\u2019s all.<br /> <br /> the immortality was pointed by Matthew in Discord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T14:09:34-07:00","id":1543702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1542097#post1542097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More on idea of <b>Gamplay Loops</b> - <a href=\"https://www.makeuseof.com/gameplay-loop-gaming/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.makeuseof.com/gameplay-loop-gaming/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to remember that &quot;gameplay loops&quot; make a lot more sense in a video game context than an RPG context.<br /> <br /> <i>Sometimes</i> they make complete sense. D&amp;D, for example, has a clear gameplay loop of &quot;Kill monsters --&gt; Get loot --&gt; Kill bigger monsters --&gt; Get better loot&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell sometimes the gameplay loop is even more tightly constrained than that. The gameplay loop of <i>Alice is Missing</i> is &quot;Spend 90 minutes exchanging in-character text messages with the other players, each of whom is playing one of six predefined characters, each of which has a predefined relationship with a girl called Alice, who is missing.&quot;<br /> <br /> But at the other end of the spectrum you have games like GURPS or even FUDGE where the first step in playing a game is to sit down and define what kind of game you're actually playing.<br /> <br /> Curseborne isn't <i>all</i> the way over to the GURPS end, but I think it's pretty far over on that end.<br /> <br /> If I was running Curseborne the first thing I'd sit down and do, without a doubt, is sit down and scribble together a campaign frame. Something to take the game from &quot;monsters exist and you are one&quot; to, say, &quot;you're a travelling circus in the dustbowl embroiled in a mystical conspiracy with apocalyptic overtones&quot; or &quot;you run a PI agency in present day New York&quot; or &quot;you're regular people in a flatshare in central London, except also you're all Accursed and also there's a weird smell in the hall and your landlord won't do anything about it and your mum's visiting and she's really judgy about this kind of thing.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T17:39:36-07:00","id":1543716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1543702#post1543702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's important to remember that &quot;gameplay loops&quot; make a lot more sense in a video game context than an RPG context.<br /> <br /> <i>Sometimes</i> they make complete sense. D&amp;D, for example, has a clear gameplay loop of &quot;Kill monsters --&gt; Get loot --&gt; Kill bigger monsters --&gt; Get better loot&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell sometimes the gameplay loop is even more tightly constrained than that. The gameplay loop of <i>Alice is Missing</i> is &quot;Spend 90 minutes exchanging in-character text messages with the other players, each of whom is playing one of six predefined characters, each of which has a predefined relationship with a girl called Alice, who is missing.&quot;<br /> <br /> But at the other end of the spectrum you have games like GURPS or even FUDGE where the first step in playing a game is to sit down and define what kind of game you're actually playing.<br /> <br /> Curseborne isn't <i>all</i> the way over to the GURPS end, but I think it's pretty far over on that end.<br /> <br /> If I was running Curseborne the first thing I'd sit down and do, without a doubt, is sit down and scribble together a campaign frame. Something to take the game from &quot;monsters exist and you are one&quot; to, say, &quot;you're a travelling circus in the dustbowl embroiled in a mystical conspiracy with apocalyptic overtones&quot; or &quot;you run a PI agency in present day New York&quot; or &quot;you're regular people in a flatshare in central London, except also you're all Accursed and also there's a weird smell in the hall and your landlord won't do anything about it and your mum's visiting and she's really judgy about this kind of thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the comparison to GURPS or FUDGE is a bit of a poor comparison because those are barely contextualized game systems, not even really trying to represent a genre just so much as <i>a</i> method of arbitration, closer to the local Storypath and Storypath Ultra rather than the particulars in terms of tweaked variations for your choice of gameline here.<br /> <br /> That said, Curseborne is primarily in the vein of &quot;self-determining characters&quot; who, at this tier, are pretty local in terms of what they're working with, akin to Requiem Vampires or Primordial Beasts*. The general jive is that what you do is decide what you want out of your characters life, try to do that, and then see how well or poorly you succeed in getting what you want. To put it another way, Curseborne doesn't give you a goal, it gives you a set of problems and you cna make your life comfortable dealing with those however you want, be it &quot;I've got a circle of people I can reliably, consensually, and non-damagingly feast on, and otherwise no other attachments that create demands for more&quot; to &quot;I am going to find out the truth of the Provenances and undo the curses of the world at the root&quot; and anywhere in between, and the rest of the game is &quot;Okay, how do you <i>do</i> that?&quot; and the fallout of each player's/character's answer.<br /> <br /> *Any attempts to claim that Curseborne is deeply like Beast the Primordial just because of this point or any of the other superficial similarities will not be treated as serious conversation and subsequently ignored, heading off wasteful conversations in future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T18:57:14-07:00","id":1543721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542047-curseborne-what-do-you-do-in-curseborne?p=1543716#post1543716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the comparison to GURPS or FUDGE is a bit of a poor comparison because those are barely contextualized game systems, not even really trying to represent a genre just so much as <i>a</i> method of arbitration, closer to the local Storypath and Storypath Ultra rather than the particulars in terms of tweaked variations for your choice of gameline here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah I agree that CB isn't as generic as GURPS or FUDGE, but I think it's far closer to that end of the spectrum than it is to the D&amp;D end in terms of how much it frames the default play experience.<br /> <br /> In this sense I don't think &quot;self determining characters&quot; is quite the distinction I'm going for. You can absolutely have self-determining D&amp;D characters and your characters in Alice is Missing are completely self determining. Similarly you can have Curseborne characters who do nothing but take orders from NPCs and solve GM-supplied problems. <br /> <br /> Like ultimately all Curseborne really tells you is &quot;Accursed exist and you are one&quot;, beyond that everything is flexible. It's technically street level but that's sort of misleading because all &quot;street level&quot; really means in this context is &quot;doesn't use any of the mechanics for going above Entanglement 4&quot;. Otherwise there's nothing intrinsically stopping you playing a game where one of the PCs is running for president.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}